    "allowance": null,
    "text": "Request or Gear check\n\nPersonal Stash can supply one Common Item without a Reserve item. Allocate mission reserves before making ordinary Gear checks or Requests.\n\nCheck \nRequest a gear pick\nGear check for a Common Item\nRequest benefit \nOrdinary Request\n Automatic Request: the GC confirms our network can fulfill this Request\n Spend one hour preparing: Sources consultation (in person/by phone) or Behind the Scenes city supporters\nSources option \nSelect only with Sources\nDossier (Sources I+)\nSkill training (Sources II+)\nLegal immunity (Sources III)\n The GC confirms this is that actual Resource option (Sources only)\nExact item or option \nReserve pick \nR: 0 remaining\nT: 0 remaining\nV: 0 remaining\nS: 0 remaining\nG: 0 remaining\nW: 0 remaining\nE: 0 remaining\nCHA: 0 remaining\nRequested category \nR\nT\nV\nS\nG\nW\nE\nRequested Caliber \nLocation \nCity, 10,000+ people: 3d20 minutes\nCity, fewer than 10,000 people: 1d6 hours\nWithin 100 miles of a city: 2d6 hours\n101–500 miles from a city: 3d6 hours\n501+ miles from a city: 4d6 hours\n We are in the field, after the Intel Phase\n Request is within my home turf: five-block urban radius or one-mile wilderness radius of home (Local Hero)\n Request: rapid communication is available\n Request: spend one full minute communicating\n Use earned Procure in a qualifying city: Request as mission Caliber +1, maximum IV, and half delivery time\n Request: the GC confirms category and Faction availability\n This Gear check is made inside my home (Personal Stash; distinct from Home Turf)\n Use Personal Stash: one Gear check per session without spending a Reserve Common Item\n Gear check: the GC confirms this is a Common Item\nShared Request funding (optional)\n\nSources uses one hour consulting contacts in person or by phone, its earned Resource option, and class level in place of Career Level.\n\nCurrent Shaken surcharge for a Request: 0 action dice, including after a class/origin cost waiver. A Request consumes its Reserve pick. Its base action-die cost equals Caliber unless a selected benefit waives that base cost. Executive Decision also succeeds automatically and ignores the mission Caliber limit (Requests remain I–IV). A Gear check consumes one Reserve Common Item. These checks have no threat/error range. Boost before resolving the result.\n\nConfirm"
